{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-338595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=0$\n- $3{y}^{″}-y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=4$\n- ${y}^{″}+y={x}^{2},\\,y(-1)=2,\\,y(1)=2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$).\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=1$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-338595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- $4{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=1$\n- ${y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,y(3)=2$\n- ${y}^{″}={x}^{3},\\,y(2)=5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition.\n\n- The second system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=3$).\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+y=x,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1$\n- ${y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=xy,\\,y(0)=3,\\,y(1)=4$\n- $2{y}^{″}+{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$).\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=2$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-130997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+4x{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3$\n- $4{y}^{″}+y=0$\n- $x{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-4$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-65012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+y=x{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=3,\\,y(4)=3$\n- ${y}^{″}-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0,\\,y(-2)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(-2)=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=4$).\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the *same* location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-2$). This is an **initial value problem.**" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-3{y}^{′}(x)+2y(x)={e}^{x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=5,\\,0\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=0$ and $x=b=2.$\n\n$$\ny(0)=1,\\,y(2)=5\n$$\n\nThese are Dirichlet boundary conditions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Dirichlet"] ["text" "Neumann"] ["text" "Other"] ["text" "Periodic"] ["text" "Robin"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Dirichlet"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+{y}^{′}(x)={x}^{3},\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3,\\,-1\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=-1$ and $x=b=2.$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\nThese are Neumann boundary conditions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74f48968130ab24e59507579f2b41f2de58f412102b9f0d51f0964a9abb1fb03"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Dirichlet"] ["text" "Neumann"] ["text" "Other"] ["text" "Periodic"] ["text" "Robin"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Neumann"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066273/state.json" "file_sha256" "2046f9e8a3a6cc2470714f5345e49ec3f604e541ce3c0d92936e476c9afc277e"} {"question" "q-338612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-y(x)={e}^{-x},\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(5)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 5\n$$\